List a boot image's ramdisk (or a ramdisk file), report its ADB properties, and with -o extract it

Usage: android-doctor ramdisk [OPTIONS] <INPUT>

Arguments:
  <INPUT>  

Options:
      --no-color         Never emit colour, even on a terminal (also honours the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -o, --output <OUTPUT>  Extract the files into this new directory (symlinks and devices are recorded, not created)
      --json             Print the result as JSON
      --list             Also list every entry
  -h, --help             Print help
